reaks down  into two categories  for extra version the two categories are  assertiveness and enthusiasm  assertiveness is a combination of  healthy confidence and  the ability to stand up for yourself and  your rights without however  disrespecting the rights of others  when you are assertive you are direct  and honest with people  you don't expect others to read your  mind about what you want  if something is bothering you you speak  up if you want or need something  you ask in simple words assertiveness is  a gentle demonstration of confident  characteristics  enthusiasm is closely related to comfort  and especially comfort in one's skin  enthusiastic people are more open and  they bring more energy to an interaction  they make friends easily reveal a lot  about themselves  and show their feelings extraversion is  essentially the positive emotion  dimension  what this means is that by being more  extroverted  you increase the probability of putting  yourself out there in the world  humans are explorers and extraversion  abets our need to dive into unfamiliar  territories  this can include more risk but also more  opportunity  the upside is that people high in  extraversion tend to form  more relationships and by doing so they  increase their social network and also  the probability of randomness and  forcing experiences upon them  both of which can prove beneficial in  succeeding in personal  and professional endeavors the downside  is that more exposure means  more vulnerability and this requires a  lot of resilience and the ability to  confront different people and views  it also means that the ego can be  inflated and that can affect their mood  behavior humility and proactivity  neuroticism can be broken down into  withdrawal and volatility  both facets of neuroticism are related  to negative emotion  and how the individual deals with it in  the case of withdrawal  the individual will internalize negative  emotion this describes people who are  anxious  depressed worry about things get easily  discouraged  become overwhelmed by events and in  general keep their psychological pain  inside them  in the case of volatility the individual  will externalize negative emotion  this describes people who are touchy  easily offended easily irritated  and demonstrate externally their  response to negative emotion  neuroticism is something very common  among humans it's like a reaction  mechanism by the body  that signals a bad situation experienced  by the individual  it's like anxiety you feel anxiety so  that you don't have to feel pain  anxiety prepares you for things that can  hurt you it is not pleasant  but it is an evolution mechanism and  because we haven't really adapted  efficiently to modern society  neuroticism is quite prevalent amongst  us to put it in different words  negative emotion determines how prone  you are to reacting negatively to the  obstacles in your path  the more you react the easier it is to  fall into depression  because you suppress your positive  emotion system and you remain stale  there is a clear indication here that  the human mind and body  are designed in a way that demands  movement the more static we become  the more negative emotion we produce  positive emotion releases dopamine which  is analgesic  meaning that it alleviates pain so what  do you do in order to reduce  neuroticism you're really high in trait  neuroticism you know so you're prone to  anxiety and  and negative emotion like you can  stabilize yourself through exposure  right so don't avoid things you're  afraid of  if especially i should be more specific  about that  if you're on a path to somewhere we've  delineated the path  and things emerged that you're afraid of  that if you avoided would compromise  your journey forward  don't avoid them break them into pieces  learn how to  in learn how to confront them and that  will strengthen you and it'll it'll  strengthen your character and it'll  lower your levels of neuroticism  but you're you're never in all  likelihood going to go from  98th percentile of neuroticism to like  second percentile  you could but you'd have to do nothing  but that your entire life and even then  it might not work so maybe if you  meditated  carefully in a tibetan retreat and you  didn't have to worry about anything else  you could  shift yourself two or three standard  deviations but  the the the amount of effort is  proportional to the movement right  so when you want to encourage  development in people  you have to find a small and performable  step forward  that constitutes improvement and point  them to that direction  this is groundbreaking and it showcases  two things  number one how prone our mind and  behavior are  to habit building and number two how  this can also be applied to a societal  scale  and affect general behavioral patterns  within the population  by choosing tangible goals that are not  extremely ambitious  you indicate to your anxiety systems  that you're more competent  then the thing is dangerous gradually  you get accustomed to the new  environment and  assuage the effect of neuroticism in  your life  in the social arena we need to form  opinions tackle problems  forge alliances and attempt to co-exist  the level of cooperation we can  establish is predicated upon how  agreeable or disagreeable we are as  people  this personality trait is called  agreeableness and it is composed of  compassion  and politeness compassion refers to how  sensitive we are to others needs and  feelings  compassionate people are more empathetic  invest in others  have a soft side and are easier to get  along with  politeness refers to how much we respect  authority  and reflects how prone we are to conform  to social norms  high agreeableness distinguishes people  who are caring  it is like the maternal aspect of their  personality  but there is an upside and a downside to  that too much agreeableness can render  one extremely dependent on others  unable to 